<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Naum of Ohrid</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 830–<a href="/years/910">910</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/9th-century">9th century</a> · Also known as Saint Naum</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Naum of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ohrid">Ohrid</a> (c. 830–910) was a Slavonic scholar and one of the disciples of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cyril-and-methodius">Cyril and Methodius</a> expelled from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/moravia">Moravia</a> in 885–886. Received in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bulgaria">Bulgaria</a> by Boris I, he taught at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/preslav">Preslav</a> and later succeeded Clement as teacher in the region of Ohrid. He founded the monastery on the shore of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lake-ohrid">Lake Ohrid</a> that bears his name and in which he is buried.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/naum-of-ohrid.jpg" alt="Naum of Ohrid" width="320" height="427" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown artist · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:SaintNaum.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
